# desk-host's pre-read list (usr/local/lib/desk-host/preread.py, ADR 0072 section 10): what a desk reads while it wakes cold, which
# `desk-host up` reads from the host's side before `runc start`, so the pages are in the page cache and charged to no desk's cap.
# Paths are relative to the slot's directory (/srv/desk-host/slots/<k>): rootfs/... is the desk's root, rel/... the host-owned release
# copies. A path with `offset+length,...` after it is read in those byte ranges only; without, the whole file. A path that isn't there
# is skipped, and a link is never followed. Order matters: deskd's files first (the hello waits for it), the root's base libraries next,
# the other services; then, after the `---` line, Chromium's, needed only at `live`: the start waits for what is above the line, and the
# rest is read beside the running desk, still capped.
# Made from a read trace of one cold free wake on an m7g.xlarge (spikes/host-wake-counters/README.md, tools/trace.sh): every file with at
# least 64 KiB resident in the page cache once the Browser was ready (mincore), with its resident page runs (runs less than 256 KiB apart
# joined). Desk image 0.3.0 on host image 0.1.5. Make it again for a new desk image: one cold wake with PREREAD=off, then trace.sh.
